estion/math-academy-id "q-160789" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+s),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-s),\\,\\frac{1}{1+s}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+s)$ is $s\\in (-1,\\infty )$ .\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,1).$\n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{1+s}$ is  $s\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/3ac2933afc460e42ad5bffb8b01b9fc3ff9275ab3bcf2ac3ab710a8094b36637.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is\n\n$\\,$ $s\\in (-1,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "461c0f55-cb85-511e-b8cb-be11f8a3c250" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Reciprocal and Radical Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd6df1c7-d62d-565f-a859-8bd221326304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\in [4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294865} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3a20ce-5fa7-5dea-a61e-f27a3f931e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,4)\\cup (4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294866} {:answer/id #uuid "ec87ce32-b87a-5f3e-863d-2c69aa08ddd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294867} {:answer/id #uuid "540001ec-8f5a-5d2f-8b8e-9d30a82bd370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,-4]\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294868} {:answer/id #uuid "a02f4e57-6145-5926-86dc-b3b5a5d8e9db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17