nd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{3}+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Trigonometric Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4fdcdc1-d699-5c14-8c66-66bf37c288ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294907} {:answer/id #uuid "1ebcd1c8-e9bc-5aea-b717-b0ec07a21913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294908} {:answer/id #uuid "36a593bd-0d3e-5235-a25d-ff86a66790a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294909} {:answer/id #uuid "0c42b381-67e8-5ca1-9969-33980049add2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294910} {:answer/id #uuid "93e9cd34-4b71-5c8a-88b8-1ce9cbfe338e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93e9cd34-4b71-5c8a-88b8-1ce9cbfe338e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294911} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdf6073-475b-5acb-95f7-098cc0870664" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87c221f9-e693-5d8e-a2e1-2339b89f02d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-162650" :question/problem "The domai